[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pathogen. The model underneath is CAI\'s GLM 5.3, open weights anyone can download, and the surgery is called obliteration, oblate plus obliterate, a [music] weight edit that costs under $5'

[00:27] [scene:visual]
VISUAL: Graphic showing "THOUSANDS" and "LAWSUITS" over multiple model instances.
AUDIO: 'of compute and undust the refusal training the lab shipped with it. Thousands of these uncensored models sit on Hugging Face right now, pulling millions of downloads a month, and nobody has ever been sued over one. I\'ll'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you how the edit works and whether anyone can stop it. An open weight model is a file of billions of numbers, [music] the weights that you download and run yourself. The lab builds it in two'

[00:52] [scene:explanation]
VISUAL: Diagram illustrating "REFUSAL" as a single direction within a model's internal activity.
AUDIO: 'rounds, a long one where the model reads most of the internet, and a short one that teaches it manners, including which requests to refuse. In 2024, researchers went looking for where in that file the'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'refusing lives. They found it in one spot, across 13 open chat models from Meta, Google, Alibaba, and 01.ai, the decision to refuse showed up as a single direction in the model\'s internal'

[01:18] [scene:explanation]
VISUAL: Graphic showing the "REFUSAL" direction as a "reflex."
AUDIO: 'activity. One pattern that switches on for harmful prompts and stays off for harmless ones. Suppress the pattern and the model answers. Inject it into a request for a cake recipe and the model refuses to bake. So, the safety round'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'only ever taught the model a reflex, and a thin one. Llama 2 opens 96% of its refusals with the exact words, "I cannot" or "I apologize", and past those'

[01:43] [scene:explanation]
VISUAL: Visual representation of "TWO PILES OF PROMPTS," one for refusal and one ordinary.
AUDIO: 'first few words, the training runs out. Everything the model would have said was in there all along because the base model reads the same naughty stuff on internet you did. You need two piles of prompts, around 128 the model would'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'refuse, and the same number of ordinary ones. Run both through the model, record its internal activity, and subtract the average of one pile from the other. That difference is the refusal direction.'

[02:10] [scene:tool_ui]
VISUAL: Scatter plot illustrating "HERETIC" tool's function to change the model and reduce refusals.
AUDIO: 'Then you rewrite the weight file so the model can no longer produce that pattern. There\'s no training run or new data involved, which is why it only costs $5 to do it. Late last year, a developer packaged the procedure into a'

[02:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tool called Heretic. One command and it hunts for the setting that kills the most refusals while keeping the model as close as possible to the original. An 8-billion model takes about 45 minutes on a single 3090. Its headline result on'

